      "releaseNotes": "Magic Mix reorders any of your playlists into an optimal arrangement, and Playback now understands the songs you've imported yourself, not just the ones from Apple Music.\n\nNew\n• Magic Mix — press and hold one of your own playlists to resequence it along Playback's similarity walk, so each track eases into the next. Preview the new order, then play it or save it.\n• Improved reliability for imported and local songs. Playback infers their genre and energy from the artist's catalogue and reads BPM straight from the file, so tracks you've added yourself surface in Songs and Design like everything else.\n\nImproved\n• Design mode now respects the songs, artists and albums you've hidden.\n• Siri and Control Center steer away from the same tracks the app does.\n• Imported album tracks stay together as the walk moves through them.\n\nFixed\n• Improved reliability for offline mode.\n• The save dialog no longer offers a stale name.\n• Fixed an overlapping banner and a mislabelled top artist.\n• Various UI fixes.",
      "version": "1.1",
      "wrapperType": "software",
      "currency": "EUR",
      "description": "Rediscover your music.\n\nPlayback spins your Apple Music library on a dial and resurfaces the songs and playlists you'd forgotten you loved.\n\nSONGS\nAn endless rotation drawn from your own library. A bespoke algorithm blends genre lineage, tempo, and sonic similarity to walk from one track to the next — prioritising the songs you've played most and those that have been in your library longest. Every queue is saved to History, so you can keep the playlists you love.\n\nPLAYLISTS\nYou've got good taste; Playback brings it to the fore. The Playlists tab spins a dial through your Apple Music playlists and lands on one at random. Your collection, reshuffled, with none of the deciding.\n\nDESIGN\nBuild a playlist by drawing its shape. Sketch an energy curve — from glacial calm up to full intensity — and Playback fills it with songs that rise and fall to match.\n\nHANDS-FREE\nEvery mode answers to your voice. Ask Siri to make a playlist, design one by mood, play something at random, or save what's playing to your library. Tap a Control Center button to start the music without unlocking your phone. It all runs on Shortcuts, so you can wire Playback into routines of your own.\n\nPRIVATE BY DESIGN\nNo accounts. No tracking. No subscription. Your music library stays on your device, between you and Apple Music.\n\nPlayback requires an Apple Music subscription.",
